{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"d8ebdf47-d995-4792-9569-a52c2019831c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"## ✅ Fix applied\n\n- **`gen.py`**: The `hr_target` function now returns `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}` instead of using the `value` key. This switches the exported HR corridor to the **Instant‑HR** mode, preventing Garmin from re‑mapping it to its own zones.\n\n- **Documentation**: All details of the change and the rationale have been recorded in **[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/d8ebdf47-d995-4792-9569-a52c2019831c/ANSWER.md)**.\n\nThe generator now produces HR corridors compatible with the expected `{start, end}` format, so watches will display the exact BPM ranges we plan.\n","duration_seconds":46.895985,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":13177,"output_tokens":2842,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":149760,"total_tokens":16019}}}
